    "section_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This section describes measurement of 'Consideration of cosmetic surgery' using the Consider subscale of the ACSS (five items), with responses on a 7-point Likert-type scale and an overall mean score computed. In the present study, Cronbach's alpha for this subscale was .92. No information on sample size, country, demographics, BMI assessment, body appreciation measures, correlations, or number of studies is reported in this section.",
      "evidence_source": "\"Consideration of cosmetic surgery was measured using the Consider subscale of the ACSS, which contains five items assessing the likelihood that a respondent would consider having cosmetic surgery.\" \"All items were rated on a 7-point Likert-type scale (1 = Strongly disagree,7= Strongly agree) and an overall score was computed by taking the mean of the five items.\" \"In the present study, Cronbach's alpha for this subscale was .92.\"",
